; The ONE variable: `reverse_fill` beside `layout_direction = 3` on a
; VFlowContainer. On a VERTICAL flow both flips land on the same axis, and
; Godot XORs them — `(rtl != reverse_fill) && vertical`
; (flow_container.cpp:248) — so setting both cancels and the columns sit
; exactly where a plain LTR flow puts them. Three columns, each a different
; width, in three containers: LTR, RTL alone (columns mirrored), and
; RTL + reverse_fill (columns back where LTR had them). An implementation
; that ORed the two flags, or that applied the mirror unconditionally, agrees
; with the middle container and disagrees with the third, which no other
; fixture can tell apart.

